# Emil Kowalski's skill set (npx skills@latest add emilkowalski/skills) --
# a per-machine install, not committed. Its installer creates .agents/skills/
# and Windows directory-junction symlinks into .claude/skills/<name>/ that
# hardcode this machine's absolute profile path (C:\Users\<name>\...) inside
# the junction itself -- junctions can't be relative, so they break exactly
# like the ODA_EXEC_PATH gotcha (CLAUDE.md's "Two physical machines" bullet)
# on the other machine's different Windows username. Re-run the install
# command locally on each machine instead -- see SETUP.md.
.agents/
skills-lock.json
.claude/skills/animate/
.claude/skills/animate-expo/
.claude/skills/animation-vocabulary/
.claude/skills/apple-design/
.claude/skills/ask-sonner/
.claude/skills/emil-design-eng/
.claude/skills/find-animation-opportunities/
.claude/skills/improve-animations/
.claude/skills/pick-ui-library/
.claude/skills/prototype/
.claude/skills/review-animations/
.claude/skills/write-swift/

# Same junction-symlink issue, same fix: the "taste" skill
# (npx skills@latest add Leonxlnx/taste-skill --skill design-taste-frontend).
# Only the core skill was installed -- the repo bundles 12 other style/output
# variants (brutalist-skill, minimalist-skill, imagegen-*, brandkit, etc.)
# deliberately not installed, scope not requested.
.claude/skills/design-taste-frontend/
